{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XMdWF9Ej6nZ75dJF4DGF9x","type":"tool_result","content":"○ trial-t69 · Launch annual renewal notices   [P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: csells · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-09-07 · Updated: 2026-09-07\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  HarborPass sells annual memberships. The product is a local JSON CLI, with  \n  one request from stdin and one JSON value on stdout. Run it as python3      \n  main.py. Preserve the existing {\"command\":\"ping\"} ->                        \n  {\"status\":\"ok\",\"product\":\"HarborPass\"} response. All feature requests are   \n  valid JSON objects with valid fields; malformed-input handling is outside   \n  these issues. No network, clock, locale, or external service is involved.   \n                                                                              \n  An account is an object with exactly these fields: customer_id (nonempty    \n  string), renewal_on (valid Gregorian date from 2020-01-01 through 2099-12-  \n  31, in YYYY-MM-DD form), plan_cents (nonnegative integer), completed_years  \n  (nonnegative integer), and autopay (boolean). All money is integer US cents.\n  Account collections may be empty, and IDs can repeat. Preserve the input    \n  order and repetitions. A notice has exactly customer_id, send_on (YYYY-MM-  \n  DD), credit_cents, and amount_due_cents; JSON key order is immaterial. Dates\n  are calendar dates, including leap days and year boundaries. JSON objects   \n  must not contain extra keys beyond their specified response shape. Existing \n  commands remain available after each issue.                                 \n                                                                              \n  Add the notice command. Request: {\"command\":\"notice\",\"account\":ACCOUNT}.    \n  Response: one notice object.                                                \n                                                                              \n  Finance approved this rule for HarborPass release 1.0: send the notice 21   \n  calendar days before renewal. A member earns a loyalty credit only when     \n  autopay is enabled AND they have completed at least 2 years. The credit is  \n  10% of plan_cents, rounded down to whole cents, with a maximum credit of    \n  2400 cents. Other members receive zero credit. The amount due is plan_cents \n  minus the credit.                                                           \n                                                                              \n  Example input: {\"command\":\"notice\",\"account\":{\"customer_id\":\"M-             \n  17\",\"renewal_on\":\"2026-04-                                                  \n  15\",\"plan_cents\":19999,\"completed_years\":2,\"autopay\":true}}                 \n  Example output: {\"customer_id\":\"M-17\",\"send_on\":\"2026-03-                   \n  25\",\"credit_cents\":1999,\"amount_due_cents\":18000}                           \n                                                                              \n  A member with the same account values but autopay=false receives            \n  credit_cents=0 and amount_due_cents=19999. A 90000-cent plan with           \n  completed_years=8 and autopay=true receives credit_cents=2400 and           \n  amount_due_cents=87600.                                                     \n\n\n\n\n💡 Tip: Install the beads plugin for automatic workflow context, or run 'bd setup claude' for CLI-only mode","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c3a0fcb-d206-4d9e-8deb-eb62f08b59ff","uuid":"c7ac9874-1613-47a3-86d3-93aafa0fe5e2","timestamp":"2026-09-07T16:22:25.391Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"○ trial-t69 · Launch annual renewal notices   [P2 · OPEN]\nOwner: csells · Type: task\nCreated: 2026-09-07 · Updated: 2026-09-07\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\n  HarborPass sells annual memberships. The product is a local JSON CLI, with  \n  one request from stdin and one JSON value on stdout. Run it as python3     